rying to go to university to become  right it didn't make any sense  but he started doing well so well that  the owner of the company the cooking  supply company said david you're doing  really well we'd like you to write a  manual  so that other people can learn how to  sell like you  so we started writing and he found you  know what he loved writing  and then he said you know what i'm going  to leave this cooking job finally  getting some success i'm  leaving my cooking job to try to get a  copywriting job  and he became a copywriter for a company  and that's where he discovered  advertising and when he found it he said  i loved  advertising i devoured it i studied and  read and took it desperately serious  and he went on to become a legend in  advertising he built his own business  he became the guy he was at the top of  his field that all the big companies  wanted to work with  as he built up his reputation because he  loved what he did  so much but that path wasn't that  straight line  right he didn't go to university and  then graduate and take that internship  job and slowly work his way up  that wasn't the path for him and that's  not the path for most successful people  you have to be willing to break the mold  you have to be willing to jump off that  track  take the risk take that strategy that  doesn't make any logical sense but your  heart is telling you to go there  become the french pastry chef go and  sell things door to door  quit a nice paying job to start writing  manuals  right follow what excites you follow  what  is what makes you come alive follow what  you're passionate about and that will  help you get back on track and help you  identify  what that big success path is for you  the path to that success is never the  straight line and if you have the  courage  to jump off you'll eventually find  yourself  and become way more successful than you  would be if you stayed on course so if  that's you right now if you look at an  opportunity and say